---
import Brand from "../../components/Brand.astro";
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { config, prices, formatPrice, deliveryText } from "../../config";
---
<Legal title="Terms of sale" description="Terms that apply when you buy an olawatch (DRAFT, needs legal review).">
  <p>
    These terms apply when you buy an <Brand name="watch" /> from us through this website as a consumer. The subscription
    service <Brand name="care" /> is covered by our <a href="/legal/subscription-terms/">subscription terms</a>. Nothing in these
    terms affects your statutory rights.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The product</h2>
  <p>
    The <Brand name="watch" /> is a wrist-worn device with an AMOLED touch display (410 × 502 pixels), built-in microphones and
    speaker, and Wi-Fi. Its AI voice assistant needs a Wi-Fi connection and an active <Brand name="care" /> subscription.
    Images on our website are illustrations until product photos are published.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Prices and payment</h2>
  <p>
    The watch costs {formatPrice(prices.watch.GBP, "GBP")} (UK) or {formatPrice(prices.watch.EUR, "EUR")} (EU),
    including VAT. Shipping costs, if any, are shown at checkout before you pay. Payment is taken by our payment
    provider, Stripe, when you place your order.
    {/* TODO(owner): confirm how VAT/OSS is shown per country and whether prices are the same in every EU country. */}
  </p>

  <h2>3. How the contract is formed</h2>
  <p>
    When you complete checkout you make an offer to buy. The contract is formed when we send you an order confirmation
    email. We may refuse an order (for example if the product is out of stock), in which case we refund you in full.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    We deliver to the United Kingdom and EU member states. Estimated delivery times: UK
    {deliveryText(config.shipping.deliveryTimes.UK)}, EU {deliveryText(config.shipping.deliveryTimes.EU)}. Unless agreed
    otherwise, we deliver within 30 days of the order confirmation. We email tracking details when your order ships.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your right to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel within 14 days after the day you (or someone you name) receive the watch, without giving a reason.
    See <a href="/legal/returns/">returns &amp; cancellation</a> for how to cancel and what happens next.
  </p>

  <h2>6. If something is wrong</h2>
  <p>
    You have legal rights if the watch is faulty or not as described: in the UK under the Consumer Rights Act 2015, and
    in the EU a legal guarantee of conformity of at least 2 years. See <a href="/legal/warranty/">guarantee &amp;
    warranty</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Our liability</h2>
  <p>
    We are responsible for loss or damage you suffer that is a foreseeable result of our breaking these terms or failing
    to use reasonable care. We do not exclude liability where it would be unlawful to do so, including for death or
    personal injury caused by negligence, or for fraud.
  </p>

  <h2>8. AI answers</h2>
  <p>
    ola's answers are generated by AI and can be inaccurate. Do not rely on them for medical, legal, financial or
    emergency decisions.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Complaints and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    Please contact us first at <a href={`mailto:${config.supportEmail}`}>{config.supportEmail}</a>. These terms are
    governed by the law of England and Wales. If you live in Scotland, Northern Ireland or the EU, you can also bring
    proceedings in your local courts and you keep the protection of the mandatory consumer law of your country.
    {/* TODO(owner): governing law, ADR scheme details, EU contact point. */}
  </p>
</Legal>
